## Scenarios

### macos smf dynlib evidence numeric guard

#### falls back when evidence numeric fields fail to parse

- Verify: falls back when evidence numeric fields fail to parse
   - Expected: gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_value(good, "p99_us") equals `"212")  # oracle: present field reads back`
   - Expected: gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_i64(good, "p99_us") equals `212i64)  # oracle: 212i64 — valid value parses`
   - Expected: gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_i64(missing, "p99_us") equals `-1i64)  # oracle: -1i64 — missing field falls back to the sentinel`
   - Expected: gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_unsigned_i64(good, "p99_us") equals `212i64)  # oracle: 212i64 — unsigned parse succeeds`
   - Expected: gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_unsigned_i64(nonnumeric, "p99_us") equals `-1i64)  # oracle: -1i64 — unsigned parse fails closed`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 11 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-GUIPERF-001
step("Verify: falls back when evidence numeric fields fail to parse")
# Runtime oracle: crafted evidence rows exercise the numeric parsers.
val good = "GUI_DYNLIB_PERF p50_us=7 p99_us=212"
val nonnumeric = "GUI_DYNLIB_PERF p50_us=7 p99_us=abc"
val missing = "GUI_DYNLIB_PERF p50_us=7"
expect(gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_value(good, "p99_us")).to_equal("212")  # oracle: present field reads back
expect(gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_i64(good, "p99_us")).to_equal(212i64)  # oracle: 212i64 — valid value parses
expect(gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_i64(missing, "p99_us")).to_equal(-1i64)  # oracle: -1i64 — missing field falls back to the sentinel
expect(gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_unsigned_i64(good, "p99_us")).to_equal(212i64)  # oracle: 212i64 — unsigned parse succeeds
expect(gui_mac_smf_dynlib_row_unsigned_i64(nonnumeric, "p99_us")).to_equal(-1i64)  # oracle: -1i64 — unsigned parse fails closed
```

